  "fresh_visual_review": {
    "fixes": [
      "Largest gap: the beacon obstructs the car and camera (drive.png t15.5). Replace the tall glowing column at the pickup with a non-occluding marker \u2014 a thin ground ring plus a short post \u2014 and fade/hide the beacon geometry when the camera is within roughly 3 m of it. The blue car and the route ahead must remain visible at t15.5.",
      "Fix camera crowding against the facade (drive.png t15.5, spawn wall in before/after.png): add camera collision that pulls the third-person camera back and raises pitch when the wall is closer than ~1.5 m, so the full car body and the fence/lane ahead are framed instead of a wall edge and car slivers.",
      "Improve actor and car readability (before.png/after.png t3.2): the gray NPC blocks and the blue sedan read as stacked prisms. Consolidate the car into one recognizable silhouette (raked cabin, visible wheels, single body mass) and give the NPCs head/shoulder and leg separation, at the same spawn positions.",
      "Repair the glazing regression from this edit (after.png t3.2): restore dark glass with a visible mullion shadow so the facade reads as windows rather than flat gray panels. No additional windows or trim \u2014 contrast only.",
      "Shrink the mission text panel that covers upper-center screen in all three frames so it no longer occludes the sky/route; keep the objective wording and anchors unchanged."
    ],
    "ok": true,
    "summary": "before.png and after.png at the identical t3.2 spawn camera differ only in window glazing: accepted dark blue-gray panes with a visible mullion became flat lighter gray slabs in after.png. That is recoloring, not a meaningful visible improvement, and it reads flatter than the accepted frame. drive.png at t15.5 shows the real remaining failure: the green objective beacon column occupies ~40% of the frame and fully hides the blue car (only roof/hood slivers visible), while the camera is jammed against the red facade so the route and fence ahead are unreadable. Regression/native data pass, but the bounded visual improvement is not demonstrated.",
    "verdict": "FIX"
  },
